  "notes": "KANJI DISTINCTION:\n- {鎮|しず}まる: for disturbances, pain, emotions, or unrest subsiding — emphasizes suppression\n- {静|しず}まる: for noise or activity becoming quiet — emphasizes silence/stillness\n\nThe transitive counterpart is {鎮|しず}める (to suppress, to calm, to quell).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\nGodan verb (intransitive). The subject is the thing that subsides (pain, anger, unrest).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {痛|いた}みが{鎮|しず}まる: the pain subsides\n- {怒|いか}りが{鎮|しず}まる: the anger dies down\n- {騒|さわ}ぎが{鎮|しず}まる: the commotion settles",
